The owner of this home is {{#field}}"field": "base/fieldTypes/owner", "display": "inline", "showLabel": false{{/field}}. The registers and controls of the home get this owner, until someone changes it. Click the owner to change it.

This home holds the security work that is done once for its scope, for example for the whole organisation, a business unit, or one team. The development projects in the scope rely on this work, and they do not repeat it. The libraries decide what work is done here. A team under an existing ISMS adds only the libraries for the work that the team does itself.

The home has these registers:

{{#report}}
  "name": "base/reports/childrenTable"
{{/report}}

The controls are in the control register, and the processes, policies, and plans are in the process register. The other registers hold the records of the work, for example the incidents, the assets, and the risks.

== What this home covers

This home is a starter kit. It sets up the security work that is done once for its scope, at a basic and proportionate level. "Basic" means that the minimum measures and their evidence are in place. It does not mean ready for certification, and it is not legal advice.

[cols="2,5,5"]
|===
| Framework | In this home | Elsewhere

| NIS2
| The governance, the cybersecurity risk-management measures of Article 21, and the reporting of Article 23, at a basic level
| The details of the national law, for example the registration and the sector rules. Check the national law.

| EU Cyber Resilience Act (CRA)
| The duties of the organisation: the channel for vulnerability reports, the notifications, and the authority contacts
| The duties for each product, for example the risk assessment, the SBOM, the technical documentation, and the conformity assessment. Do them in the development projects of the secure development and EU CRA modules.

| ISO/IEC 27001
| A foundation: the scope, the policy, the roles, the assets, the risks, the targets, and the reviews
| Certification: the Statement of Applicability, the internal audit, the full management review, the corrective actions, and the full Annex A. These are in the ISO/IEC 27001 extension.
|===

The section "Libraries" shows what each library covers.

